invariant: INV-46
file: src/mlkem.c
catches: test/mlkem-builds.sh
reason: mlkem.c's message expansion calls mlkem_poly.c's loop in a host
  object, so every session reads each bit of the message through a
  volatile object. Nothing else objects: the loop writes the same
  coefficients, and only the time is wrong. The script compiles mlkem.c as
  a host object does and requires it to call mlk_vector_frommsg and not
  mlk_poly_frommsg.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    mlk_vector_frommsg(p, msg);
--- new
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    mlk_poly_frommsg(p, msg);
